      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While protein is great for energy, you need to be very careful with some high-protein foods when taking MAOIs. Aged cheddar and salami are cured, which can contain tyramine, a substance that can cause a dangerous blood pressure spike when combined with MAOIs. Soy sauce should also be approached with caution as it can contain fermented ingredients. It is best to discuss specific food restrictions with your healthcare provider or a dietitian who is knowledgeable about MAOI dietary restrictions.",
      "source": "target",
